rationale:
Split. The supplied proof has four independent layers:
(i) measure-theoretic locality of approximate tangent planes (steps 1–2: a growth bound from Definition 1.4, then Besicovitch's density theorem), used three times;
(ii) linear algebra: two unit orientations of one plane differ by a sign (step 3);
(iii) construction of the combined triple (M', θ', ξ') and verification of every IMRep field (steps 3–5);
(iv) integration (step 6).

The seven children follow this structure:
- tangent_growth = step 1;
- tangent_locality = step 2;
- imrep_tangent_transfer = the double locality application used in steps 3 and 5;
- orientation_sign = the orthonormal-basis/determinant argument of step 3;
- overlap_orientation_sign = the conclusion of step 3;
- combination_construction = steps 3–5;
- combination_action = step 6.

Parent assembly from children 6 and 7:
1. From IsIntegerMultiplicity T₁ and T₂ obtain R₁ and R₂.
2. combination_construction gives R with 1_{M'}θ'ξ' = p₁1_{M₁}θ₁ξ₁ + p₂1_{M₂}θ₂ξ₂ Hⁿ-a.e.
3. combination_action gives R.action ω = p₁R₁.action ω + p₂R₂.action ω.
4. Hence S ω = p₁T₁ ω + p₂T₂ ω = R.action ω, so R represents S.

This assembly is checked in Lean against the exact frozen parent type:
- It compiles using only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound, plus sorryAx from the child stubs.
- The glue proofs (imrep_tangent_transfer from tangent_locality; overlap_orientation_sign from imrep_tangent_transfer and orientation_sign) also compile.
- orientation_sign has a complete sorry-free Lean proof that follows the supplied natural proof.

Two departures from the parent's wording, both stated in the child proofs:
- tangent_locality is step 2 with the parent's ambient locally finite set taken to be the large set itself. This holds in every application.
- combination_construction uses the Borel sign σ = 1 on {ξ̃₂ = ξ̃₁} and −1 elsewhere, instead of the coordinate test Σ_I⟨e^I,ξ₁⟩⟨e^I,ξ₂⟩ ≥ 0. That test needs Cauchy–Binet, which Mathlib lacks. Only ξ̃₂ = σξ̃₁ a.e. on M₁ ∩ M₂ is used.

The tangent_locality type is string-identical to regcomp_approx_tangent_locality on another branch. That node is not accepted yet, so a fresh name is used. All names carry the unused prefix rsdic_.

tangent_locality and combination_construction are the heavy children and may be split further at depth 3.
